cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, its formal proofs, software, figures, or research results, please cite Jeromie N. Beasley and the relevant paper/release DOI when available."
title: "Operator-First research master"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Beasley"
    given-names: "Jeromie N."
repository-code: "https://github.com/dicipler-pixel/operator-first"
# Zenodo archive. Replace the placeholder with the concept DOI Zenodo issues on
# the first release; the concept DOI resolves to the newest version forever, so
# it never needs changing again. Per-release DOIs go under `identifiers`.
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
abstract: >-
  Formal proofs, research notes and instrumentation from the Operator-First
  research programme: Lean formalizations audited to a fixed trust base, the
  Compound Eye instrument and its append-only hash-chained event ledger, the
  two-adic counting lemma and exact n-step Syracuse digit law, and
  Andrews-Curtis corridor search tooling. The logic, theories, planning and
  research direction are the author's; mathematical assistance was provided by
  AI systems and is credited as assistance, not authorship.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - operator theory
  - spectral projectors
  - formal verification
  - Lean
  - mathematical physics
  - Compound Eye
  - Collatz
  - 2-adic valuation
  - Syracuse map
  - Andrews-Curtis
  - axiom auditing
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ac-square-divisibility"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Sneiderman"
        given-names: "Robert"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Robby955/ac-square-divisibility"
    notes: >-
      Commit d0ed2c06. Cited wherever root-conjugacy, donor-restoration,
      coordinate-transport, divisibility, period or companion-restoration ideas
      are used.
